`replay --namespace` (#612, FJ5; spike S13, r4 §4.1).

A replayer stands in for the owners it recorded: it republishes under their
original addresses, in a namespace of its own where they are not running.
`--namespace` opens the session in that namespace and moves every key there
from the capture's base. The fixture was recorded under base `prod`: two
samples of `host-a/tc`'s bandwidth stream, and one foreign key.

```console
$ zenctl replay --dry-run --format table --color never --namespace replay tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec
tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec: captured prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** under base "prod" (2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
would put replay/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0  (12 B, application/json)
would put replay/legacy/temperature  (2 B, text/plain)
would put replay/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0  (12 B, application/json)
would replay 3 put(s) and 0 tombstone(s) from prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** (captured 2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
into namespace "replay", each key moved from the capture's base "prod"

```

Replaying a zk2 service's own key into the namespace it was recorded in —
where its owner runs — would write a key the owner owns (P3, spec §6), and
each such row is refused and counted unless `--i-know`. Foreign rows replay
as before. A refused row is the act failing, so it exits 1.

```console
$ zenctl replay --dry-run --format table --color never --namespace prod tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec
? 1
tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec: captured prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** under base "prod" (2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
refused prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in namespace "prod", the one it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
would put prod/legacy/temperature  (2 B, text/plain)
refused prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in namespace "prod", the one it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
would replay 1 put(s) and 0 tombstone(s) from prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** (captured 2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
into namespace "prod", each key moved from the capture's base "prod"
  prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in namespace "prod", the one it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
  prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in namespace "prod", the one it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
0 malformed row(s), 2 refused row(s) — counted, not silently skipped

```

```console
$ zenctl replay --dry-run --format table --color never --namespace prod --i-know tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec
tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec: captured prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** under base "prod" (2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
would put prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0  (12 B, application/json)
would put prod/legacy/temperature  (2 B, text/plain)
would put prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0  (12 B, application/json)
would replay 3 put(s) and 0 tombstone(s) from prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** (captured 2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
into namespace "prod", each key moved from the capture's base "prod"

```

Without `--namespace`, every key is published as recorded, which is the
namespace it came from:

```console
$ zenctl replay --dry-run --format table --color never --base prod tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec
? 1
tests/cmd/fixtures/zk2.zrec: captured prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** under base "prod" (2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
refused prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in the namespace it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
would put prod/legacy/temperature  (2 B, text/plain)
refused prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in the namespace it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
would replay 1 put(s) and 0 tombstone(s) from prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/** + prod/legacy/** (captured 2026-10-08T00:00:00Z)
  prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in the namespace it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
  prod/zk2/host-a/tc/tc.netif.v1/stream/bandwidth/default/eth0: is a key host-a/tc owns, and would land in the namespace it was recorded in, where its owner runs: only the owner writes its keys (P3, spec §6). Replay into a namespace of your own with --namespace, or pass --i-know to write it anyway.
0 malformed row(s), 2 refused row(s) — counted, not silently skipped

```
